Show the workspace's own processes in the web Resource Manager

Resource Manager showed all zeros in the tile: the web preload's
`memory.getSnapshot` was an empty-snapshot stub. It now routes to the runtime's
`diagnostics.memory` method, which paired phones already poll, so the tile
reports the workspace host's processes and its RAM and CPU. The empty snapshot
survives only as the fallback for when no environment is connected.

To test, open Resource Manager in the tile and confirm it lists the workspace's
processes rather than zeros. Covered by `web-preload-api.test.ts`.

